			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young woman in <Picture 1>, with long brown hair, a black top, small earrings, and a warm smiling expression.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video presents <Subject 1> dancing gracefully over five seconds. Her identity, hairstyle, clothing, and facial features come from <Picture 1>. The scene uses soft stage lighting against a dark background, with a slow camera push-in to emphasize her movement and smile.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the woman's long brown hair, black top, earrings, facial features, and smiling expression are retained from <Picture 1>.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses a realistic stage-performance style with soft frontal lighting and a dark, slightly blurred background.\n[Shot 1] The shot opens on a medium close-up of <Subject 1>, the young woman with long brown hair falling past her shoulders, wearing a black top and small earrings. She faces the camera with a warm smile, her lips gently parted as if mid-expression. As the five-second clip unfolds, she begins to dance: her head tilts softly to one side, then returns to center; both hands rise slowly from below the frame to chest height, fingers relaxed, palms facing inward. Her shoulders roll in a smooth circular motion, and her torso sways gently left and right with each beat of an implied rhythm. The camera performs a slow, steady push-in toward her face, tightening the framing from medium close-up to a closer portrait by the final second. Background lights remain as soft bokeh points of white and blue, shifting subtly in brightness. Her hair moves naturally with each head turn, catching the light along its edges. By the last moment, she completes one full sway cycle, hands settling back below frame level, her smile broadening slightly as she holds eye contact with the lens.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA low ambient stage hum and faint reverb tail persist throughout the five seconds; no physical action sounds are prominent.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
			],
